     1	"""TweakSpec — the typed DEFINITION layer for owner controls (P9A).
     2	
     3	Tweaks are the small set of knobs the platform exposes to a non-technical owner (toggle a
     4	phone field, pick a curated accent, set a count). This module defines what a tweak IS — its
     5	editor + constraints — separately from the current VALUES (``AppSpec.tweaks``). P9B persists
     6	``.disco/tweaks.json``, P9C's ``app_set_tweak`` validates a value against this schema, P9D
     7	renders the TweakPanel. Pure, frozen value objects + validation; no runtime imports.
     8	
     9	Design rules (gpt-5.5-gated): a tweak must be GROUNDED — it controls behavior or >=1 field;
    10	a TEXT/COLOR tweak must control behavior or >=2 fields (single-place copy/color belongs in
    11	app_update_content / app_set_design, not a tweak). Numeric bounds are exact (integer-scaled,
    12	never float modulo); colors are a strict #RGB/#RRGGBB hex subset normalized to #rrggbb;
    13	palettes are 2-5 unique curated swatches and a value must be one of them.
